          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em basic line bundle on the 2-sphere
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line+bundle"} complex line bundle
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sphere"} 2-sphere
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
            is a generator
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ±
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm 1 \in \mathbb{Z} \,\simeq\, H^2(S^2, \mathbb{Z})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tautological+line+bundle"} tautological line bundle
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+sphere"} Riemann sphere
            regarded as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+projective+space"} complex projective 1-space
          %p
            This is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+bundle"} pullback bundle
            of the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2 \to B U(1) \simeq B^2 \mathbb{Z}
            to the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+space"} Eilenberg-MacLane space
            which itself represents a generator of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_2(S^2) \simeq \mathbb{Z}
          %p
            Beware that this basic line bundle is sometimes called the “canonical line bundle on the 2-sphere”, but it is
            %em not
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
            to what in complex geometry is called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+bundle"} canonical bundle
            of the 2-sphere regarded as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theta+characteristic"} theta characteristic
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization+of+the+2-sphere"} geometric quantization of the 2-sphere
          %p
            The basic line bundle is the canonically
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated bundle
            to basic
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundle"} principal U(1)-bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+Hopf+fibration"} complex Hopf fibration
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tautological+line+bundle"} tautological line bundle
            for the complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+space"} projective line
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℙ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{C})
            (the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+sphere"} Riemann sphere
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ∖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℙ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^2 \setminus \{(0, 0)\} \to \mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{C})
            mapping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x, y)
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo ;
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [x; y]
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundles"} principal U(1)-bundles
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundles"} associated bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line+bundles"} complex line bundles
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BU%28n%29"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B U(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmannian"} Grassmannian
            is the infinite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+projective+space"} complex projective space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of this space is that of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+space"} Eilenberg-MacLane space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\mathbb{Z},2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\mathbb{Z},2)
            is in particular
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path-connected+topological+space"} path-connected
            and has second
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
            the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_2(K(\mathbb{Z},2)) \simeq \mathbb{Z}
          %p
            It being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            for complex line bundles means that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mtext isomorphism classes of
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mtext complex line bundles
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mtext on
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 2
                    %mo }
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mtext continuous functions
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mtext up to homotopy
                    %mo }
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  \\text{isomorphism classes of}
                  \\\
                  \\text{complex line bundles}
                  \\\
                  \\text{on}\,\, S^2
                  }
                  \\right\}
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  \\text{continuous functions}
                  \\\
                  S^2 \longrightarrow K(\mathbb{Z},2)
                  \\\
                  \\text{up to homotopy}
                  }
                  \\right\}
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  \\pi_2(K(\mathbb{Z},2))
                  \\;\simeq\;
                  \\mathbb{Z}
                  \\,.
          %p
            The (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+class"}> isomorphism class
            ) of the complex line bundle which corresponds to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} +1 \in \mathbb{Z}
            under this sequence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            is called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em basic complex line bundle on the 2-sphere
          %p
            Hence the basic complex line bundle on the 2-sphere is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+bundle"} pullback bundle
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+complex+line+bundle"} universal complex line bundle
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BU%28n%29"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B U(1)
            along the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2 \to B U(1)
            which represents the element
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \in \mathbb{Z} \simeq \pi_2(B U(1))
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BU%28n%29"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B U(1)
            is represented by the infinite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+projective+space"} complex projective space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^\infty
            with its canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
            structure (
            %a{:href => "complex+projective+space#CellComplexStructureOnComplexProjectiveSpace"}> this prop.
            ), then this map is represented by the canonical cell inclusion
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2 \hookrightarrow\mathbb{C}P^\infty
          %p
            Notice that there is a non-trivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism"} automorphism
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            given by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \mapsto -n
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#general General
          #ClutchingConstructionOfBasicLineBundle.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/clutching+construction"} clutching construction
                of the basic line bundle)
            %p
              Under the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/clutching+construction"} clutching construction
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
              on the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sphere"} 2-sphere
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transition+function"} transition function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{C} \supset \, S^1 \longrightarrow GL(1,\mathbb{C}) \, \subset \mathbb{C}
            %p
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1 \subset \mathbb{R}^2 \simeq \mathbb{C}
              to the complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
              in 1-dimension, which is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo ∖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(1,\mathbb{C}) \simeq \mathbb{C} \setminus \{0\}
              given simply by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi z
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    z \mapsto z
                    \\,,
            %p Alternatively, due to the sign ambiguity in the definition of the basic bundle, its clutching transition function is given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi z
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    z \mapsto - z
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Under the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/clutching+construction"} clutching construction
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+class"} isomorphism class
              of a complex line bundle corresponds to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+class"} homotopy class
              of its clutching transition function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo ∖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^1 \to GL(1, \mathbb{C}) \simeq \mathbb{C} \setminus \{0\}
            %p
              hence to an element of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo ∖
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(\mathbb{C} \setminus \{0\}) \simeq \mathbb{Z}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ±
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm 1  \in \mathbb{Z} \simeq [S^1, GL(1,\mathbb{Z})]
              and this element is represented by the function
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi z
                      %mo ↦
                      %mo ±
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \mapsto \pm z
          #TensorRelationForBasicLineBundleOn2Sphere.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong (fundamental tensor/sum relation of the basic complex line bundle)
            %p
              Under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum+of+vector+bundles"} direct sum of vector bundles
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \oplus_{S^2}
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+vector+bundles"} tensor product of vector bundles
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes_{S^2}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \to S^2
              satisfies the following relation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 2
                    %mi H
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi H
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 2
                      %mi H
                      %mo )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H \oplus_{S^2} H
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\left(
                    H \otimes_{S^2} H
                    \\right)
                    \\oplus_{S^2}
                    1_{S^2}
            %p
              (where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_{S^2}
              denotes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+vector+bundle"} trivial vector bundle
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line+bundle"} complex line bundle
              on the 2-sphere).
          %p
            (e.g (
            %a{:href => "#Hatcher"}> Hatcher, Example 1.13
            ))
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Via the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/clutching+construction"} clutching construction
              there is a single
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transition+function"} transition function
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^1 \longrightarrow GL(n,\mathbb{C})
            %p
              that characterizes all the bundles involved. With
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1 \hookrightarrow \mathbb{C}
              identified with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspace"} topological subspace
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
              of unit
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+value"} absolute value
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+vector+bundle"} trivial
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundle"} line bundle
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_{S^2}
                  we may choose
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi z
                        %mo ↦
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1 \colon z \mapsto \left( 1 \right)
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  for the basic line bundle we may choose (by lemma
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClutchingConstructionOfBasicLineBundle"}
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi H
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi z
                        %mo ↦
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mi z
                          %mo )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_H \colon z \mapsto \left( z\right)
            %p This yields
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi H
                        %mo ⊕
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \otimes H \oplus 1_{S^2}
                  the clutching function
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi z
                        %mo ↦
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mrow
                            %mtable
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %msup
                                    %mi z
                                    %mn 2
                                %mtd
                                  %mn 0
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %mn 0
                                %mtd
                                  %mn 1
                          %mo )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \mapsto \left( \array{ z^2 &amp; 0 \\ 0 &amp; 1 }\right)
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                        %mo ⊕
                        %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \oplus H
                  the clutching function
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi z
                        %mo ↦
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mrow
                            %mtable
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %mi z
                                %mtd
                                  %mn 0
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %mn 0
                                %mtd
                                  %mi z
                          %mo )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \mapsto \left( \array{ z &amp; 0 \\ 0 &amp; z }  \right)
                  \.
            %p
              Since the complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Gl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gl(n,\mathbb{C})
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path-connected+topological+space"} path-connected
              (by
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "general+linear+group#ConnectednessOfGeneralLinearGroup"} this prop.
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\gamma \colon [0,1] \longrightarrow GL(2,\mathbb{C})
            %p
              connecting the identity matrix on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^2
              with the one that swaps the two entries, i.e.
            %p
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mn 1
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma(0) = \left( \array{ 1 &amp; 0 \\ 0 &amp; 1 }  \right)
            %p
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma(1) = \left(  \array{ 0 &amp; 1 \\ 1 &amp; 0 } \right)
            %p Therefore the function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ×
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi GL
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 2
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ℂ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi z
                            %mo ,
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AA
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mrow
                                %mi H
                                %mo ⊕
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi z
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mi γ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⋅
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mrow
                                %mn 1
                                %mo ⊕
                                %mi H
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi z
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mi γ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^1 \times [0,1] &amp;\overset{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; GL(2,\mathbb{C})
                    \\\
                    (z,t)
                    \&amp;\overset{\phantom{AA}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    f_{H \oplus 1}(z) \cdot \gamma(t) \cdot f_{1 \oplus H}(z) \cdot \gamma(t)
                    }
            %p
              (with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+multiplication"} matrix multiplication
              on the right) is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                        %mo ⊕
                        %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_{H \oplus H}
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mrow
                          %mi H
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi H
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_{H \otimes H \oplus 1}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+product+theorem+in+topological+K-theory"}> fundamental product theorem in topological K-theory
                )
            %p Under the map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo ∼
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Vect(S^2)_{/\sim} \longrightarrow K(X)
            %p
              that sends
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+bundles"} complex vector bundles
              to their class in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
              ring
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X)
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TensorRelationForBasicLineBundleOn2Sphere"}
              says that the K-theory class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              of the basic line bundle in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X)
              satisfies the relation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi H
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msup
                              %mi H
                              %mn 2
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                            %mo −
                            %munder
                              %munder
                                %mrow
                                  %mn 2
                                  %mi H
                                %mo ⏟
                              %mrow
                                %mo =
                                %msup
                                  %mi H
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    (H - 1)^2
                    \&amp; =
                    H^2  + 1 - \underset{= H^2 + 1}{\underbrace{2 H}}
                    \\\
                    \= &amp;   0
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X)
            %p
              (Notice that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H-1
              is the image of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [H]
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+K-theory"} reduced K-theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde K(X)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2
              under the splitting
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X) \simeq \tilde K(X) \oplus \mathbb{Z}
              (by
              = succeed ").)" do
                %a{:href => "topological+K-theory#KGrupDirectSummandReducedKGroup"} this prop.
            %p
              It follows that there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+homomorphism"} ring homomorphism
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi h
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi h
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mn 2
                              %mo )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi h
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↦
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AAA
                          %mtd
                            %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{Z}[h]/\left( (h-1)^2 \right)
                    \&amp;\overset{}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    K(S^2)
                    \\\
                    h &amp;\overset{\phantom{AAA}}{\mapsto}&amp; H
                    }
            %p
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+ring"} polynomial ring
              in one abstract generator,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+ring"} quotiented
              by this relation, to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
              ring.
            %p
              It turns out that this homomorphism is in fact an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
