          %p
          #RelationToChernInsulators.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (relation to Chern insulators)
              The normalized Hamiltonians
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SphereParameterizedHamiltonian"} (1)
              play a key role in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid+state+physics"} solid state physics
              in the discussion of 2D 2-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electron+band"} band
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crystals"} crystals
              such as notably considered as models for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+insulators"} Chern insulators
              (like the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haldane+model"} Haldane model
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "Chern+insulator#SticletEtAl12"} Sticlet et al 2012 (2-3)
            %p It follows from the above discussion that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  any continuous family of such operators over a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brillouin+torus"} Brillouin torus
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi T
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^2
                  is given by a continuous map
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %msup
                            %mi T
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon T^2 \longrightarrow{} S^2
              %li
                %p
                  the +1 eigenspace bundle of the corresponding family of operators on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi T
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^2
                  (the
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valence+bundle"} valence bundle
                  in these models) has
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
                  equal to the pullback along
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
